# Live-session-only packages of the cham3 M1 image. They are installed in live-build's
# "live" pass, so live-build lists them in live/filesystem.packages-remove and the
# image's debian-installer removes them from an installed system. (live.list.chroot,
# which lists nothing, stops lb config from installing live-boot and live-config in the
# "install" pass, where the installer would keep them.)
#
# live-boot, live-config, live-config-systemd: the live system's boot and configuration.
# user-setup: live-config creates the live account ("user", live-config's public
# default password "live") only when this package is installed (its 0030-user-setup
# component exits early otherwise), and SDDM's live autologin into the Plasma Wayland
# session (live-config 0085-sddm plus cham3's 0086-cham3-sddm-wayland) needs that
# account. It is only a Recommends of live-config, and the image is built with
# --apt-recommends false, so without it the first native M1 image booted to the SDDM
# greeter with no live user (VM gate, m1_image run 38203029813).
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd
user-setup
